        "generated suite: 11 failed / 5 passed of 16 executed; the 5 passes are exact-multiple and input-validation controls"
      ],
      "hypotheses": [
        "page_count truncates the partial final page, and has_next_page inherits the error, hiding items that slice_page would serve correctly"
      ],
      "investigations": [
        "swept total_items 0-13 at per_page=3 and compared against ceiling division: disagreement occurs in exactly the cases where total_items % per_page != 0",
        "compared page_count against ceiling division across per_page in {2,3,5} and total_items 0-19: 39 of 60 cases disagree, all with a non-zero remainder",
        "checked reachability directly: summing len(slice_page(...)) over pages 1..page_count loses exactly total_items % per_page items",
        "confirmed slice_page(items, 4, 3) == [9] in isolation, so the partial page is served correctly and only the count is wrong"
      ],
      "root_cause": {
        "status": "confirmed",
        "explanation": "page_count uses floor division (total_items // per_page), so any remainder is truncated and the partial final page is never counted. has_next_page derives its bound from page_count, so the 'next' control stops early and those items become unreachable even though slice_page would return them. When total_items < per_page the count is 0 and the entire listing disappears."
      },
